1.WATER TANKS 
You are given an integer array tank[], where tank[i] represents the initial amount of water (in liters) in the i-th tank. 
Each tank has an unlimited capacity, but due to municipal regulations, no tank can hold more than x liters of water.

You have an unlimited supply of empty tanks available to store water. You can transfer only whole integer amounts of water between tanks. 
During the transfer, if you transfer less than or equal to w liters, all the transferred water will be wasted. If you transfer more than w liters, 
only up to w liters will be wasted, and the remaining water will be successfully transferred.

The goal is to maximize the total amount of water remaining across all tanks after the transfers, ensuring:

No tank holds more than x liters.
SOURCE CODE : 
        class Solution {
            public long remWater(int[] tanks, int x, int w) {
                long sum=0;
                long loss=0;
                for(int water:tanks){
                    if(water<x){
                        sum+=water;
                    }
                    else{
                        sum+=x;
                        long extra=water-x;
                        long transfer=extra/(x+w);
                        long rem=extra%(x+w);
                        sum+=transfer*x;
                        sum+=Math.max(0,rem-w);
                    }
                }
                return sum;
            }
        }
